## .NET / Visual Studio build output
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/
aprx*

# Visual Studio cache/options
.vs/

# User-specific files
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Esri add-in packages (binary output produced by the ArcGIS Pro SDK)
# *.esriAddinX
*.esriAddin

# MSBuild logs
*.binlog
*.log

*.gdb

# MkDocs build output (docs_dir is docs-src/, site_dir is docs/) and local virtualenv. The
# GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/docs.yml) builds and deploys docs/ to GitHub
# Pages -- it's never committed.
docs/
# Pre-built stand-alone downloader bundled into the add-in (see KylidarAddin.csproj) -- the one
# build output that IS committed, so a fresh clone can build the add-in without first publishing
# tools\KylidarDownloader. Everything else under that project's bin/obj stays ignored.
!tools/KylidarDownloader/bin/
tools/KylidarDownloader/bin/*
!tools/KylidarDownloader/bin/publish-win-x64/
tools/KylidarDownloader/bin/publish-win-x64/*
!tools/KylidarDownloader/bin/publish-win-x64/KylidarDownloader.exe
